spans.s:
ज॑नन f. ई = जनक a.;
 m. progenitor, creator, f.
ई mother;
 n. producing, causing;
 birth, life.

जनपद॑ m. district, country (lit. tribe-place);
 (also
pl.) people, esp. country people, subjects (opp. prince).

जा॑नपद a. living in the country;
 m. countryman (in
both mgs), subject.

ज॑नस् n. race;
 as indecl. (also जनर्) N. of a cert.
world.

ज॑नि f. woman, wife, pl. metaph. the fingers;
 जनि also
birth, origin, birthplace.

ज॑नी f. woman, wife, pl. metaph. the fingers;
 जनि also
birth, origin, birthplace.

जनि॑त्र n. birthplace, home, origin;
 pl. parents,
relatives.

ज॑निमन् n. birth, origin;
 offspring, descendants;
creature, being;
 race, kind.

जनु॑स् n. birth, origin, birthplace;
 creature, being;
creation, production, work;
 race, kind. Instr. जनु॑षा by birth or
nature, essentially, necessarily.

जन्तु॑ m. creature, being, any animal, esp. worms, insects,
etc.;
 man, person (sgl. also coll.);
 attendant, servant;
 child,
descendant.

ज॑न्मन् n. birth, origin, new birth;
 existence, life;
birthplace, home;
 progenitor, father (esp. —˚ begotten by);
 creature,
being;
 relatives, people i.g.;
 race, kind;
 nature quality.

1 जन्य a. born, produced, rising from (—˚);
 abstr. ˚ता
f., ˚त्व n. — n. body.

2 ज॑न्य a. belonging to the (same) race, national, native;
common, vulgar. — m. the bridegroom's friend;
 f. आ bridesmaid;
 n.
people, tribe, race (also जन्य॑), pl. inimical tribes;
 fighting, war.
